Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:23:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Canary upload + catalog publish: administrator MetaMask
 handoff (source only, inactive)

Upload: the administrator personal_signs exactly enclave-upload:<component sha256>:<expiry>;
this local server recovers the signer, trades the signature once for a relay token, posts the
one pinned 101222-byte file, requires the gateway's CID to equal the pinned CID and the bytes
fetched back by that CID to hash to the pin. Durable journal before every side effect; the
signature is never stored or logged; unanswered uploads reconcile by fetch, never blindly.
Publish: gated on a fresh fetch-back; the reviewed read-only preparer (ad81dd5, vendored
byte-identical) re-runs at every prepare; reviewed transport (fb189e46) plus gate, upload
routes and a chain-based reconcile (evidence/handoff-server.diff); exact-field hash accept;
two-provider verification with event and getApp/getVersion readback. Port 39675; the
factory handoff is untouched. Tests on anvil with the deployed catalog/book runtimes and a
fake relay/gateway: handoff 11/11, browser 2/2 (464 MiB), mutants 15/15.
